      <image>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Linuxuser67/Grab/v4.5.9/data/screenshots/new-download-format.png</image>
    </screenshot>
    <screenshot>
      <caption>Live stream recording alongside active downloads</caption>
      <image>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Linuxuser67/Grab/v4.5.9/data/screenshots/live-recording.png</image>
    </screenshot>
  </screenshots>
  <releases>
    <release version="6.3.1" date="2026-10-24">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Hardened media network handling by scoping redirect DNS policy and keeping proxy configuration alive for the full request lifecycle.</li>
          <li>Bound browser-cookie staging and aligned browser profile selection, while hardening cookie serialization and redacting sensitive details.</li>
          <li>Improved CI reproducibility by pinning media tools used by tests.</li>
          <li>Refactored asynchronous media lookup to keep network and extraction work separated from GTK card state.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="6.3.0" date="2026-10-23">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>YouTube extraction now provisions the latest stable Deno release.</li>
          <li>Gallery-dl installs and updates now use the official stable Codeberg release, verifying the Linux executable against its published SHA256SUMS file before installation.</li>
          <li>Live HLS capture accepts generic HTTPS .m3u8 manifests as a fallback when the native HLS protocol is unavailable.</li>
          <li>Media-tool probes share cached results and run asynchronously to reduce repeated subprocess launches and keep the GTK interface responsive.</li>
          <li>Queue restoration, file reconciliation, and shutdown use explicit lifecycle guards and move blocking work off the GTK main thread; failed restores preserve the saved queue.</li>
          <li>Live recordings that fail final MP4 remuxing due to timestamp or trailer errors retry with constrained stream mapping and timestamp recovery options.</li>
          <li>Improved startup URL handoff, scheduler wakeups, process cleanup, browser-extension cookie staging permissions, and gallery-dl proxy handling.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="6.3.0~beta.2" date="2026-10-23">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Media URL lookup now logs phase timings for yt-dlp tool checks, JavaScript runtime readiness, metadata extraction and parsing, plus gallery authentication and lookup. Both probes and existing routing behavior are preserved to help measure latency before further performance changes.</li>
          <li>Live recordings that fail final MP4 remuxing due to timestamp/trailer errors now retry with constrained video/audio mapping and timestamp recovery options.</li>
          <li>Quit now hides the window immediately while bounded asynchronous cleanup finishes, and an in-progress queue restore no longer delays shutdown indefinitely or overwrites the saved queue.</li>
          <li>Fixed AppStream version lookup for prerelease builds.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="6.3.0~beta.1" date="2026-10-23">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Live HLS capture now accepts generic HTTPS .m3u8 manifests as a fallback when the native HLS protocol is unavailable.</li>
          <li>Media-tool version and capability probes run asynchronously and share cached results, reducing repeated subprocess launches and keeping the GTK interface responsive.</li>
          <li>Queue restoration, file reconciliation, and shutdown now use explicit lifecycle guards and move blocking work off the GTK main thread; failed restores preserve the saved queue.</li>
          <li>Improved startup URL handoff, scheduler wakeups, process cleanup, and regression coverage for startup and shutdown races.</li>
          <li>Updated the ctutils security dependency to version 0.4.4.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="6.2.2" date="2026-10-23">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Live streams reported through yt-dlp's live status are now detected correctly instead of taking the finished-video path.</li>
          <li>Large download queues are saved more compactly, reducing the risk of the saved queue being set aside at startup.</li>
          <li>Browser-extension cookie handoffs now enforce owner-only staging-directory permissions, including directories left readable by earlier versions.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="6.2.1" date="2026-10-22">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Improved gallery-dl proxy handling across previews, counts, collection selection, and downloads, including discovery of Grab-managed tools by delegated downloaders.</li>
          <li>Improved handling of selected HLS cases, including live .fmp4 segments, and routed unfamiliar gallery file types to the all-files picker.</li>
          <li>Added validated yt-dlp extractor-specific arguments for site workarounds, with sensitive argument values redacted from debug output.</li>
          <li>Unconfirmed browser handoffs now fail closed when a configured proxy prevents Grab from enforcing its destination-safety checks.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="6.2.0" date="2026-10-22">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Security: unconfirmed browser handoffs now restrict extractor traffic to public destinations, fail closed when the destination cannot be pinned safely, and redact sensitive URL details from diagnostics.</li>
          <li>Gallery and collection selections now refresh the download queue when returning to the main window.</li>
          <li>Live HLS recordings retry transient segment-open failures instead of skipping affected segments.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="6.1.2~beta.1" date="2026-10-22">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Gallery and collection pickers now refresh the download queue when returning to the main window, so newly selected items appear immediately.</li>
          <li>Live HLS recordings now retry transient segment-open failures instead of skipping the affected segment.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="6.1.1" date="2026-10-21">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Browser-extension handoff now reports how many cookies Grab accepts, allowing compatible extensions to warn when cookies are excluded by the target URL's scope or path.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="6.1.0" date="2026-10-21">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Gallery and collection pickers handle large result sets more reliably and adapt their layout to small selections.</li>
          <li>Grab no longer downloads or manages FFmpeg: Flatpak builds use FFmpeg and ffprobe from the app or GNOME runtime, while other builds use the system PATH.</li>
          <li>Hardened browser-cookie handoff and media-tool state checks to avoid stale state and improve missing-tool handling.</li>
          <li>Updated TLS certificate dependencies and refreshed compatible Rust dependencies.</li>
          <li>Made manual proxy settings easier to find in Preferences.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="6.0.2~beta.7" date="2026-10-21">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Gallery pickers now adapt their column count to small result sets, avoiding unused space when fewer than three items are available.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="6.0.2~beta.6" date="2026-10-21">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Stop downloading and managing FFmpeg: Flatpak builds resolve FFmpeg and ffprobe from the app or GNOME runtime, while other builds use the system PATH.</li>
          <li>Update TLS certificate dependencies for current WebPKI security advisories.</li>
          <li>Keep manual proxy settings directly below the proxy-mode selector.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="6.0.2~beta.5" date="2026-10-20">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>FFmpeg and ffprobe installation now recognizes BtbN's current checksum-bearing Linux builds, fixing rejection of the upstream stable-branch filename format.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="6.0.2~beta.4" date="2026-10-20">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Fresh Flatpak profiles now reliably offer installation until Grab-managed yt-dlp, FFmpeg, and ffprobe are present.</li>
          <li>Browser-cookie handoff avoids stale cookie snapshots being paired with a newer user agent, and stale asynchronous tool checks can no longer overwrite newer state.</li>
          <li>Gallery and collection pickers improve submission-state handling and selection-count coverage for very large result sets.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="6.0.2~beta.3" date="2026-10-20">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Video-tool setup now installs a static FFmpeg build that includes both ffmpeg and ffprobe.</li>
          <li>Missing ffprobe triggers a repair offer, and downloaded tool archives are verified before installation.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="6.0.1" date="2026-10-19">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>More reliable gallery and playlist downloads, including improved backend selection, authentication handoff, retries, and cancellation.</li>
          <li>Large gallery, playlist, and torrent pickers now stream entries and use virtualized grids for more responsive selection.</li>
          <li>Improved collection-entry naming, download progress handling, and gallery workflow reliability.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.17" date="2026-10-19">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>File pickers: entries in the recycling grids now keep an even space between rows and columns.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.16" date="2026-10-19">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>The recycling-grid file pickers got some breathing room: entries no longer touch between rows and columns.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.15" date="2026-10-19">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>The playlist, torrent and gallery file pickers moved to a recycling grid: entries stream in with no height limit, and the picker keeps the count, multi-select (clicks, Ctrl+A, a rubber band from empty space) and Enter toggles the focused row.</li>
          <li>Gallery runs cap per-line stderr and metadata reads, so a broken or hostile extractor can no longer inflate memory with one oversized line.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.14" date="2026-10-18">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>The New Download card now lives in the content area instead of the toolbar, avoiding toolbar sizing problems with tall gallery and playlist pickers.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.13" date="2026-10-18">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Button pills in the file pickers wrap to fit their own text, video page headings show a count-only subtitle, and gallery enumeration no longer stops at 5000 files.</li>
          <li>Preferences → Media describes the support tools as yt-dlp and gallery-dl only; the row shows readiness, no versions.</li>
          <li>Adding short links (youtu.be/…) reuses the lookup's info JSON at download time, skipping the redundant re-extraction and easing YouTube rate limits.</li>
          <li>A failed subtitle fetch no longer fails the video: the download retries once without subtitles.</li>
          <li>Live HLS capture pins yt-dlp's ffmpeg downloader, which is the only one that can record live m3u8 streams.</li>
          <li>The first yt-dlp spawn of a session now carries the browser TLS impersonation flag; the support probe runs at startup.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.12" date="2026-10-18">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Gallery folders and headers name the collection itself instead of the first file, and downloaded playlist entries use their own titles.</li>
          <li>Cancelling a gallery download now really terminates the gallery-dl process, and gallery lookups no longer hang or balloon memory on unusual pages.</li>
          <li>Gallery rows restored after a restart keep their collection subfolder, so Delete works on them again.</li>
          <li>Removed the mis-drawn Done checkmark that painted over the row's media icon.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.11" date="2026-10-18">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Gallery-dl video and gallery results now wait for file selection before they are queued.</li>
          <li>YouTube extraction explicitly keeps the default player-client rotation while excluding the problematic web client.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.10" date="2026-10-18">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Gallery submits (Enter, Add, tick icon, and auto-add) open the file picker instead of queueing every file.</li>
          <li>Subtitle resolution reuses the probe info JSON, so it no longer re-runs the lookup.</li>
          <li>Update checks run only from the Check for Updates button: opening the Media section and app launch no longer check.</li>
          <li>The failure dialog returns to its previous size.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.9" date="2026-10-17">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Fixes a crash when looking up gallery links.</li>
          <li>Remote .torrent links are fetched on the network runtime.</li>
          <li>Live recording remux files are namespaced per download, so cleanup never removes another download's files or your own files.</li>
          <li>A failed high-quality remux retries the simpler remux instead of stalling.</li>
          <li>Downloads never overwrite a file that appears when the download starts.</li>
          <li>Update checks are cached: a manual check reuses results from the last 15 minutes, and the startup check queries upstream at most once a day.</li>
          <li>Startup notice when a newer yt-dlp is available.</li>
          <li>yt-dlp failures caused by extractor breakage suggest updating yt-dlp.</li>
          <li>gallery-dl updates are judged by the installed binary; a system gallery-dl is not offered an update.</li>
          <li>Tool downloads use the same guarded DNS resolver as file downloads.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.8" date="2026-10-17">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Gallery picker opens as soon as the first file is listed, so large galleries no longer wait for the full listing.</li>
          <li>Gallery picker lists up to 5000 files, up from 500, and stays responsive at that size.</li>
          <li>Gallery picker shows a note when a selection may be out of date because the gallery changed.</li>
          <li>Link lookups run both gallery-dl and yt-dlp and choose the result from what they actually found.</li>
          <li>Deleting a gallery download removes its folder only when Grab created it.</li>
          <li>Closes a symlink race when writing private metadata files.</li>
          <li>Gallery enumeration failures now include gallery-dl's error output in the log.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.7" date="2026-10-16">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Gallery operations no longer freeze the UI during probe, count, or cookie export.</li>
          <li>Gallery probe and count now use the browser's User-Agent for authenticated sites.</li>
          <li>Failed gallery downloads keep cookies for retry; partial failures are retryable.</li>
          <li>Multi-file torrent picker no longer triggers browser download deletion.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.6" date="2026-10-16">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Instagram gallery probes and downloads now throttle requests to avoid rate limits.</li>
          <li>Browser extension handoff now distinguishes queued downloads from opened cards.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.5" date="2026-10-16">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>gallery-dl probe now uses the browser extension's cookies ("Download with Grab").</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.4" date="2026-10-16">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Fix a crash when gallery-dl probes a URL (missing Tokio runtime).</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.3" date="2026-10-16">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Check for Updates now offers to install missing tools (gallery-dl, quickjs).</li>
          <li>Completed downloads show a checkmark badge on the row icon.</li>
          <li>gallery-dl now probes when yt-dlp fails with unsupported-URL or login-required errors (e.g. Instagram stories).</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.2" date="2026-10-16">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Speed limit now uses single-fragment downloads with the full cap instead of dividing across fragments.</li>
          <li>Gallery probe recognizes more formats (HEIC/HEIF, FLV, WMV, and others); filters match classification.</li>
          <li>Direct media links skip the gallery probe when yt-dlp can't handle them.</li>
          <li>Gallery filter counts no longer write into replaced cards; failed counts are cached per filter.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.9~beta.1" date="2026-10-15">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Cookie handoff: playlist items use same-host fallback, browser UA applied.</li>
          <li>Origin-only Referer sent on downloads.</li>
          <li>Per-attempt cookie jar accepts Set-Cookie.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.8" date="2026-10-14">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Dependency refresh to latest stable.</li>
          <li>Torrent icons (rows and preferences) use a plain symbolic icon.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.5" date="2026-10-14">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Unauthenticated handoffs now wait for the user's confirmation instead of queueing silently.</li>
          <li>Handoff cookies: direct downloads use handoff cookies, staged before queueing to avoid races.</li>
          <li>Extension only gets acceptance once Grab actually queues the URL.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.5~beta.2" date="2026-10-14">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Unauthenticated handoffs now wait for the user's confirmation instead of queueing silently.</li>
          <li>Handoff cookies: direct downloads use handoff cookies, staged before queueing to avoid races.</li>
          <li>Extension only gets acceptance once Grab actually queues the URL.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.5~beta.1" date="2026-10-13">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Extension async confirm: the handoff no longer holds a 130s connection, fixing MV3 worker timeouts.</li>
          <li>LL-HLS timestamp hygiene on all HLS downloads, fixing intermittent ffmpeg failures.</li>
          <li>Cookie handoff hardening: truncate to 100 instead of rejecting, stage before queueing.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.4" date="2026-10-13">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Browser extension pairing: the extension now verifies Grab via a shared secret before sending cookies, so session cookies only go to the real Grab. Pairing code is in Preferences → Advanced.</li>
          <li>Extension cookie handoff: the browser extension can now hand off site cookies with downloads, fixing logins on protected sites.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.4~beta.2" date="2026-10-13">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Browser extension pairing: the extension now verifies Grab via a shared secret before sending cookies, so session cookies only go to the real Grab. Pairing code is in Preferences → Advanced.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.4~beta.1" date="2026-10-13">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>The browser extension can now send site cookies with a download handoff, letting yt-dlp pass Cloudflare bot challenges. Cookie scope (host-only, path, secure, expiry) is preserved.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.3" date="2026-10-11">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Fixed torrent status showing "Starting torrent…" after pausing and resuming a download that was already in progress.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.2" date="2026-10-11">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Torrent downloads now show what they're doing while starting: fetching metadata, finding peers, or connecting.</li>
          <li>Dependency updates.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.1" date="2026-10-10">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Security fixes: Host/Origin validation on extension server, bounded handoff queue (429 when full), DNS guard at connect time.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.0" date="2026-10-10">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Browser extension integration over local HTTP (replaces native messaging).</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.0~beta.2" date="2026-10-09">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Browser extension now uses HTTP (127.0.0.1:9412) instead of native messaging — no setup needed, works from Flatpak.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.7.0~beta.1" date="2026-10-09">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Browser extension tries native messaging first, falls back to grab:// URLs.</li>
          <li>Dependency updates (zstd-sys); cc stays pinned at 1.5.1.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.6.9" date="2026-10-09">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Stopping a DASH download merges parts into a single file.</li>
          <li>VOD HLS downloads use a single file instead of fragments.</li>
          <li>Dependency updates.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="5.6.8" date="2026-10-09">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Stopping a DASH download merges parts into a single file.</li>
          <li>VOD HLS downloads use a single file instead of fragments.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
